      <!-- ── THE BRIEF ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="cs2-section reveal">
        <h2 class="cs2-section__label">The brief</h2>

        <div class="cs2-row">
          <h3 class="cs2-row__label">The problem</h3>
          <div class="cs2-row__body">
            <p>Nuad Thai Spa Kathmandu grew from a single location to four branches the way most service businesses do &ndash; one good year at a time, with the booking system never catching up. Appointments were confirmed over the phone, tracked branch by branch, and reconciled against the till at the end of the day. It worked with one branch to watch. It stopped working at three.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Mornings spent calling each branch manager to find out who was booked and what had been collected</li>
              <li>Discounts agreed verbally, so a 15% off could go unnoticed until the numbers didn&rsquo;t add up</li>
              <li>Staff moved between branches informally &ndash; a manager found out only when the client was already waiting</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs2-row">
          <h3 class="cs2-row__label">What changed</h3>
          <div class="cs2-row__body">
            <p>Zennly replaced the phone-and-spreadsheet system with a single operational layer across all four branches. Every booking now moves through the same lifecycle &ndash; Pending, Confirmed, In-Progress, Completed &ndash; visible in real time to whoever is allowed to see it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

