      <!-- ── BEFORE → AFTER ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="cs2-section reveal">
        <h2 class="cs2-section__label">Before &rarr; after</h2>

        <div class="cs2-map">
          <div class="cs2-map__avatar" aria-hidden="true">NT</div>

          <div class="cs2-map__quad">
            <h3 class="cs2-map__h3">Booking &amp; scheduling</h3>
            <p>Front-desk staff create bookings directly against a specific therapist and room. Conflicts are prevented at the database level, not caught after the fact by a manager comparing notebooks.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="cs2-map__quad">
            <h3 class="cs2-map__h3">Discount control</h3>
            <p>A therapist can still offer a discount &ndash; but it&rsquo;s a request, not a decision. It only applies once a manager approves it, and every request carries the exact percentage and amount.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="cs2-map__quad">
            <h3 class="cs2-map__h3">Staff transfers</h3>
            <p>When a therapist moves between branches, it&rsquo;s a scheduled event with an effective date &ndash; not a phone call the morning of. Managers at both branches see the change coming.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="cs2-map__quad">
            <h3 class="cs2-map__h3">Daily reconciliation</h3>
            <p>Every payment is logged at the point of service, against the booking it belongs to. The owner&rsquo;s morning call round is now a single dashboard that&rsquo;s already correct.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── THE RESULT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
